---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'November 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How CheatCodeGTAVI.com handles data: what we collect, what we don't, and how to contact us about it."
>
  <PageHero eyebrow="Legal" title="Privacy Policy" subtitle={`Last updated ${lastUpdated}.`} accent="gold" />

  <div class="mx-auto flex max-w-3xl flex-col gap-8 px-5 py-14 text-text-secondary sm:px-8 sm:py-20" data-reveal-group>
    <div data-reveal class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-heading-sm text-text-primary">Summary</h2>
      <p class="text-body-md">
        CheatCodeGTAVI.com collects the minimum data needed to run its features. This site displays ads and uses
        Google Analytics (see below) to help cover hosting costs and understand traffic; we don't sell your data to
        anyone. This page describes exactly what is collected and why.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div data-reveal class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-heading-sm text-text-primary">Email addresses (launch notifications)</h2>
      <p class="text-body-md">
        If you sign up for a launch notification via the "Notify Me" form, we store your email address so we can
        send you a one-time notification when GTA 6 cheat codes go live. We do not use this address for any other
        marketing, and we do not share it with third parties. Every launch email includes an unsubscribe link, and you can
        also ask us to delete your address at any time (see Contact below).
      </p>
    </div>

    <div data-reveal class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-heading-sm text-text-primary">Contact form</h2>
      <p class="text-body-md">
        If you send a message through the contact form, we store the message and any name or email address you choose
        to include so we can read it and reply. We use a one-way hash of your IP address only to limit spam, and we
        delete messages on request.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div data-reveal class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-heading-sm text-text-primary">Site search</h2>
      <p class="text-body-md">
        Search runs in your browser against a list of pages that is downloaded to your device. What you type is not
        sent to us.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div data-reveal class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-heading-sm text-text-primary">Favorites</h2>
      <p class="text-body-md">
        Cheats you save to your Favorites list are stored only in your browser's local storage. This data never
        leaves your device and we never see it — clearing your browser data or using a different device/browser
        will reset your favorites.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div data-reveal class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-heading-sm text-text-primary">Voting</h2>
      <p class="text-body-md">
        After launch you can report whether a cheat code worked. To stop one person voting many times, we store a
        one-way hash of your IP address next to your vote. The hash can't be turned back into your IP address, and we
        never store the address itself. Votes are shown only as totals, and we don't connect them to your name or
        email address.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div data-reveal class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-heading-sm text-text-primary">Hosting and standard logs</h2>
      <p class="text-body-md">
        This site is hosted on Cloudflare's network, which, like virtually every host on the internet, processes
        standard connection metadata (IP address, request timing, user agent) to serve pages and protect against
        abuse. We do not run any social-media advertising trackers (e.g. Meta Pixel) on this site — our only
        advertising and analytics partner is Google, described below.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div data-reveal class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-heading-sm text-text-primary">Advertising (Google AdSense)</h2>
      <p class="text-body-md">
        This site displays ads served by Google AdSense to help cover hosting and pipeline costs. Google and its
        advertising partners use cookies and similar technology to serve ads based on your visits to this and other
        sites, and to measure ad performance. Google may use this data to personalize the ads you see. You can
        control the ads Google shows you, or opt out of personalized advertising entirely, at <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" class="text-accent-secondary hover:text-accent-secondary/80" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Ads Settings</a>, and third-party vendors' use of cookies is described in Google's <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" class="text-accent-secondary hover:text-accent-secondary/80" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Advertising Partners policy</a>. We don't control what specific ads are shown or receive your personal data from the ad network.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div data-reveal class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-heading-sm text-text-primary">Analytics (Google Analytics)</h2>
      <p class="text-body-md">
        We use Google Analytics (GA4) to understand aggregate traffic — which pages get read, roughly how many
        visitors we get, and what device/browser they're on. Google Analytics sets cookies and collects your IP
        address and usage data to do this; that data is processed by Google under its own <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" class="text-accent-secondary hover:text-accent-secondary/80" target="_blank" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a>. We use this data in aggregate only — we don't use it to identify individual visitors, and we don't combine
        it with the email addresses collected for launch notifications. You can opt out of Google Analytics
        tracking site-wide using a browser extension like <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" class="text-accent-secondary hover:text-accent-secondary/80" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's opt-out add-on</a>, or by using a browser/extension that blocks third-party analytics scripts.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div data-reveal class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-heading-sm text-text-primary">Cookies</h2>
      <p class="text-body-md">
        We don't set our own tracking or advertising cookies directly. Google Analytics and Google AdSense (see
        above) set their own cookies to distinguish visitors and serve/measure ads. Your theme preference
        (light/dark), saved favorites and your own vote choices are stored in your browser's local storage on your
        device, not in cookies, and are not sent to us.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div data-reveal class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-heading-sm text-text-primary">Children's privacy</h2>
      <p class="text-body-md">
        This site is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from
        them.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div data-reveal class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-heading-sm text-text-primary">Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p class="text-body-md">
        If how we handle data changes, we'll update this page and the "Last updated" date above.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div data-reveal class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-heading-sm text-text-primary">Contact</h2>
      <p class="text-body-md">
        Questions about this policy, or want your data deleted? Email <a href="mailto:contact@cheatcodegtavi.com" class="text-accent-secondary hover:text-accent-secondary/80">contact@cheatcodegtavi.com</a> or visit our <a href="/contact/" class="text-accent-secondary hover:text-accent-secondary/80">Contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
